  "details": "<p>Ballance (1951: 99) discusses the so-called \"Ponte Apollosa\" as a possible close parallel to the Ponte Cadaro on the Via Flaminia. In footnote 75, Ballance notes that the Latin inscription (<em>CIL\u00a0</em>9, 2122) that records a bridge restored under Septimius Severus and Caracalla in 198 CE is generally associated with the\u00a0<span>\"</span><span>Ponte Apollosa\" has a provenance that is not completely certain.</span></p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Ponte Apollosa, a bridge of the Via Appia that may have been restored by Septimius Severus in 198 CE.",
